The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
ret = plat_dat->init(pdev, plat_dat->bsp_priv);
if (ret)
    return ret;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because if the `init()` function fails after the hardware initialization, the probe function does not call the `exit()` callback to clean up resources, which can lead to resource leaks or inconsistent states in the driver.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
ret = stmmac_dvr_probe(&pdev->dev, plat_dat, &stmmac_res);
if (ret)
    goto err_exit;
...
if (plat_dat->exit)
    plat_dat->exit(pdev, plat_dat->bsp_priv);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces error handling after the `stmmac_dvr_probe()` call. If an error occurs, it jumps to the `err_exit` label, where it checks if the `exit()` callback is defined and calls it to properly clean up resources, ensuring that the driver does not leave resources allocated in case of an error.

